In terms of their chemical and physical properties, Caesium-137 and Caesium-133 are isotopes of the same element (caesium), which means they have the same chemical properties. However, Caesium-137 is a radioisotope with a high nuclear decay rate, whereas Caesium-133 is a stable isotope.

