1.  **De-Stalinization**: The Soviet Union, under Nikita Khrushchev, implemented de-Stalinization, which included denouncing Joseph Stalin and revising Marxist-Leninist doctrine. Albania, under Enver Hoxha, perceived this as contrary to Marxist-Leninist doctrine and an opportunistic act to legitimize revisionism.
